      "side": 1,
      "message": "I’ll have to disagree here. The LFS servlet registration is happening in core Gerrit [1].\n\nThe plugin never even sees this request, so there’s nothing to fix in the LFS code path. The request gets swallowed within core Gerrit.\n\nSo I believe the options we have are:\n* preventing new repositories to be made with certain prefixes (but this doesn’t fix previously made repositories)\n* Reorder the servlet order (but this is fragile, a bug can be introduced upon reordering)\n\nWere you potentially thinking about the plugin’s `AllRequestFilter`? This might be able to be configured in just the LFS plugin and essentially skips the servlet routing.\n\n[1] https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/tags/v3.15.0/java/com/google/gerrit/httpd/plugins/HttpPluginModule.java#37",
